      "side": 1,
      "message": "filenames can\u0027t be inferred in following cases:\n\n1) package name: an interface or parcelable defined in pkg.name package can be at xxx/yyy/pkg/name/IFoo.aidl. We can\u0027t sure that the output would be \u003cout\u003e/xxx/yyy/pkg/name/[I|Bn|Bp]Foo.h.\n\n2) when a single AIDL file has multiple types in it (not here but in aidl_interface), we can\u0027t even infer basename of the file.\n\n3) When the input is parcelable, the Bn* and Bp* headers are not created. (Note: we are currently generating the headers but they are meaningless and thus shouldn\u0027t be created)",
